# Claude Code — personal/local overrides (e.g. autoMemoryDirectory). Never committed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Codex — the project-local config is machine-specific (it names absolute interpreter paths outside
# this workspace entirely) and is NOT the permission layer. `.codex/rules/*.rules` IS the permission
# layer and IS tracked, deliberately, from skills#419 on. The exclusion is written here rather than in
# `.git/info/exclude`, which is where both of those files sat until that Issue: that file is per-clone
# and unversioned, so `git status` hid them, no PR ever contained them, and nothing anywhere recorded
# that hiding them had been decided. A rule about what this repository does not track belongs in a
# tracked file.
.codex/config.toml
